{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427803-extra-senses-which-sphere-s-needed","id":1427803,"title":"Extra senses, which Sphere(s) needed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-08T20:36:25-08:00","id":1427803,"title":"Extra senses, which Sphere(s) needed?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am curious as to what sphere(s) and the rating needed to get extra senses, in this example seeing infrared. My ideas were: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Forces 1 alone to perceive infrared.</li> <li>Forces 1 and Life 2. Because you are affecting yourself and need Life 2 for that.</li> <li>Forces 1 and Life 3. Because you are <i>altering </i>yourself and need Life 3 for that.</li> <li>Life 3. To copy the vision/senses of the Bullfrog or the Pit Viper.</li> <li>Life 3 and Forces 1. To be <i>able </i>to copy the vision/senses of the Bullfrog or the Pit Viper.</li> <li>Life 3. To modify (somehow) your eyeballs and brain and see infrared.</li> <li>Life 3 and Forces 1. To <i>able </i>to modify (somehow) your eyeballs and brain and see infrared.</li> </ol><br /> Which option, if any, is correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 12-08-2020, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T23:16:09-08:00","id":1427813,"title":"","content":"Forces 1 alone lets you sense heat. Life 3 alone lets you modify your body to have animal traits. Everything else is a Sphere tax, and don't let anyone tell you otherwise.<br /> <br /> Which you prefer depends on what Sphere dots your character has at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T04:59:30-08:00","id":1427841,"title":"","content":"There is often more than one way to do things, just remember to always use the lowest sphere combination you can think of for each way. Only options 1 and 6 qualify, and if you are only determining sphere cost by results rather than process, only option 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T05:34:59-08:00","id":1427848,"title":"","content":"6 and 1.<br /> 1 To see infrared.<br /> 6 Some animals can see infrared, and you can copy animal senses with Life 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T11:25:56-08:00","id":1427882,"title":"","content":"1, 4/6, or 7:<br /> <br /> 1) You don't need to modify your body to modify your senses, you can just use Forces, even with PBD.<br /> <br /> 4/6) You don't need Forces to give yourself existing real animal features, but there are limitations to what naturally occurring infrared senses can do compared to what Forces can accomplish. These two options are fundamentally the same, pick whichever fits your Focus.<br /> <br /> 7) If you don't want to stick to Life (higher levels of Life can exceed Life 3's limitations). The reason to pick this over #1 is to avoid the difficulty increase for juggling multiple effects. This is ST dependent because when effects count towards juggling or not is largely a ST call with little solid guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T11:56:12-08:00","id":1427887,"title":"","content":"Any sphere 1.<br /> <br /> Every sphere allows you to &quot;Sense&quot; things related to that sphere outside your normal senses as long as your paradigm allows it. For example: Correspondence gives you a 360 degree awareness around yourself that could apply to sight, sound, taste, etc, or could be an entirely alien sense that makes you aware of that area somehow. The only thing defining this is your mage's paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T04:53:21-08:00","id":1427957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427803-extra-senses-which-sphere-s-needed?p=1427882#post1427882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1, 4/6, or 7:<br /> <br /> 1) You don't need to modify your body to modify your senses, you can just use Forces, even with PBD.<br /> <br /> 4/6) You don't need Forces to give yourself existing real animal features, but there are limitations to what naturally occurring infrared senses can do compared to what Forces can accomplish. These two options are fundamentally the same, pick whichever fits your Focus.<br /> <br /> 7) If you don't want to stick to Life (higher levels of Life can exceed Life 3's limitations). The reason to pick this over #1 is to avoid the difficulty increase for juggling multiple effects. This is ST dependent because when effects count towards juggling or not is largely a ST call with little solid guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh, somehow I missed 4. Yes, that would work too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}